18. Consistency audit
Architecture: The plan preserves routes/controllers/use cases/repositories/models and does not add a browser-side mutation owner.
Security: The plan preserves HttpOnly cookie authority, CSRF, tenant scope, high-risk permission, self-review denial, no credential storage, and fail-closed errors.
Data: The plan uses the existing approval row, payload integrity, idempotency, audit, and canonical POS/Inventory execution. No destructive data operation is proposed.
Frontend boundaries: The plan targets standalone POS and shared web-core only where the POS terminal already consumes it; IMS is explicitly excluded and tested for non-regression.
Production: The plan treats the observed stale live artifact as a hard rollout blocker and does not claim that main or a merged commit is deployed.
Phase numbering: The plan uses the next authoritative number, Phase 353, and preserves all historical numbering.
Documentation: The plan cites the authoritative architecture and governance docs, ADR 0086, API/database/testing docs, and current implementation paths. Reference-only Back Office documentation is used as context, not as a higher authority than the ADR or architecture docs.
